{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1521050-need-advice-on-planning-a-mystery","id":1521050,"title":"Need advice on planning a mystery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-20T12:22:47-07:00","id":1521050,"title":"Need advice on planning a mystery","content":"I've got an idea for a game I want to run, where I want to send my players after a collection of necromancy-inscribed skulls, loosely based on the Skull Diary from 2nd Edition, that have been rediscovered in Sijan. A graverobber found one of the skulls, hocked it with a pawnbroker that happened to be the agent of a Lunar shahan-ya, and then got caught by the Black Watch. The graverobber was then executed and then his ghost imprisoned in Sijan's Underworld reflection. The players will be tasked with retrieving the skulls before anyone else gets their hands on them.<br /> <br /> I expect that my players first thoughts will be to try to find the tomb where this first skull came from in order to find some clue as to where the other skulls are. I know that the tomb's former occupant is part of a small society of First Age necromancer-scholars, most of which were entombed in Sijan. What I don't know is what clues to leave in the tomb so that the players can start tracking down the other skulls.<br /> <br /> Any suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T22:31:04-07:00","id":1521098,"title":"","content":"My first thought was to play around with grave goods. Do you want to have a trip to the underworld? If that is interesting, then have evidence in the tomb that the necromancer-scholar was buried there with his journals. The cracked remnants of the journal's cover remain, but the pages inside have long since disintegrated into dust. But when an item is left as a grave gift in Creation, an idealized version of it is created in the underworld. So if the players go into the underworld (easy enough in Sijan), they could track down the copy of the journals there. That could be a single fairly straight-forward sub-plot, or maybe the journals have been traded or captured or otherwise moved, and it turns into a longer task, however complicated you want to make it. Once they find the correct journal, it identifies the other members of the society who had the other skulls. Maybe some of them died prior to the author and their tombs were identified (either clearly, or just hinted at) so they will be a little easier to find, while others only have their names in the journal, so the party has to investigate what happened to those scholars and where they might be buried.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26886-lindharin","name":"Lindharin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-26T06:27:52-07:00","id":1521426,"title":"","content":"Sorry, who are the PCs? What have they got going for them here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-28T11:41:10-07:00","id":1521522,"title":"","content":"Currently, I've only got two of the PCs concepts and partial character sheets. There may be a third. All will be Lunars. Of the two I have, one is a monster hunter inspired very much by the witcher and the other is planning a femme fatale socialite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T21:55:27-07:00","id":1521729,"title":"","content":"Consider where the other skulls are, how long ago they left, if they left all at once, and at least some of the route they've taken.<br /> <br /> Figuring out clues will be easier if you know where they are then you can figure out what to leave to point in that direction. Knowing if they left all at once, one at a time, or in chunks will make timelines a bit easier to work with, and the routes are because it will go best if they aren't all at say the first merchant the person tried selling them to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T05:04:20-07:00","id":1522263,"title":"","content":"Thanks for answering, I appreciate you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28130-maricastaneda","user":"MariCastaneda","date":". 10-12-2023, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28130-maricastaneda","name":"MariCastaneda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}